# Vercel deploy exclusion.
#
# dist/server.js is the rosezm *application* module (render/db/schema, 39 named
# exports, no default export). It exists for the edge adapter
# (src/cli/edge.ts createEdgeHandler -> import(outDir + '/server.js')), NOT for
# the Vercel lambda: the lambda entrypoint (index.js) loads dist/prod.mjs, which
# is self-contained and imports only node builtins plus ./client.js.
#
# It MUST stay out of the lambda bundle. The bundle keys files by basename and
# names the entry handler server.js, so shipping dist/server.js makes it collide
# with - and win over - the real entry: /var/task/server.js then resolved to the
# 39-named-export module and every request failed at cold start with
#   Invalid export found in module "/var/task/server.js".
#   The default export must be a function or server.
dist/server.js
dist/server.js.br
